 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/sports/college-football-playoff-viewers-guide.html', 'snippet': 'Ten teams can claim to have a chance to make the playoff entering this weekend’s conference championship games, but clarity might come early on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Entering this weekend’s major-conference, neutral-site championship games, only 10 teams have any kind of shot at the four-team College Football Playoff.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/sports/02colleges1/merlin_130719320_4d32487e-b819-455e-8007-b5a1f28e9754-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/02/sports/02colleges1/merlin_130719320_4d32487e-b819-455e-8007-b5a1f28e9754-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/sports/02colleges1/merlin_130719320_4d32487e-b819-455e-8007-b5a1f28e9754-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/sports/02colleges1/merlin_130719320_4d32487e-b819-455e-8007-b5a1f28e9754-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/sports/02colleges1/02colleges1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/02/sports/02colleges1/02colleges1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/sports/02colleges1/02colleges1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Viewer’s Guide to This Weekend’s College Football Playoff Drama', 'kicker': 'On College Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Championship Day May Settle Playoff Debate Early On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Football Playoff National Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clemson University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oklahoma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auburn University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Georgia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Miami', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Christian University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Southern California', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-01T12:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bdb48c9-2876-5b3e-8a51-75046e1941f8', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bdb48c9-2876-5b3e-8a51-75046e1941f8'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Tifrere spends much of her day with her 10-year-old son, Kasseem, often using the High Line to walk to art galleries, restaurants and skate parks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/nyregion/how-mashonda-tifrere-art-and-hip-hop-maven-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Tifrere spends much of her day with her 10-year-old son, Kasseem, often using the High Line to walk to art galleries, restaurants and skate parks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reality television fans might know Mashonda Tifrere as a former cast member on “Love & Hip Hop: New York.” Music fans might know her from the songs she’s collaborated on with Jay-Z, Eve and DMX. But currently, Ms. Tifrere, 38, is committed to ArtLeadHER, an organization she created that is dedicated to promoting women artists. In addition to organizing shows, including “King Woman,” an exhibition of 25 contemporary women artists currently on view through Dec. 9 at Pen + Brush in the Flatiron district, Ms. Tifrere gets involved in the business side of art, helping women artists sell their works to her collector friends, who include the singer/songwriter Maxwell and the basketball player Carmelo Anthony. Ms. Tifrere splits her time between a home in Fort Lee, N.J., where she has her own modern art collection, and a one-bedroom apartment in Chelsea. She lives with her son, Kasseem Dean Jr., 10, and their dog, Chloe. Most Sundays, mother and son avoid the suburbs and roam the city.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03routine-1/merlin_129429713_02c0d914-7af2-4c0e-9cbb-6b4facd4cea5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03routine-1/merlin_129429713_02c0d914-7af2-4c0e-9cbb-6b4facd4cea5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03routine-1/merlin_129429713_02c0d914-7af2-4c0e-9cbb-6b4facd4cea5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03routine-1/merlin_129429713_02c0d914-7af2-4c0e-9cbb-6b4facd4cea5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03routine-1/03routine-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03routine-1/03routine-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03routine-1/03routine-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Mashonda Tifrere, Art and Hip-Hop Maven, Spends Her Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hip-Hop Maven, Gliding Along', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tifrere, Mashonda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'High Line (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-01T12:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tammy La Gorce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tammy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d908c8e5-aa3a-544d-a5a4-f83e18ee144b', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d908c8e5-aa3a-544d-a5a4-f83e18ee144b'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s program applies to managers but omits a vast majority of workers, like teachers, police officers and park rangers, who are in unions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/nyregion/paid-parental-leave-except-for-most-who-need-it.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s program applies to managers but omits a vast majority of workers, like teachers, police officers and park rangers, who are in unions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago this month, Mayor Bill de Blasio made an announcement from which he has mined political capital ever since: That employees of the City of New York would receive paid parental leave, an ostensibly progressive policy in line with those established in cities like Austin and Pittsburgh. Given that only 13 percent of employees in the private sector in this country get any kind of compensated leave to care for young children, this was considered a laudable investment in sanity. There was, however, a crucial fine-print dimension to the order. By “employees,’’ the mayor was referring only to those 20,000 or so public workers belonging to the managerial class and not the hundreds of thousands of other individuals — educators, lunchroom attendants, police officers, librarians, park rangers, computer programmers, court reporters and so on — who are represented by unions and make up a vast majority of the municipal labor force.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03BIG/03BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03BIG/03BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03BIG/03BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03BIG/03BIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03BIG/03BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03BIG/03BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/nyregion/03BIG/03BIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paid Parental Leave, Except for Most Who Need It', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parental Leave Omits Teachers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'na