cle/57f820e7-0e2f-5d41-95c0-1144ac22425c'}, {'abstract': 'He met with Muslim refugees and heard their stories, but did not address his earlier public silence about them while in Myanmar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/world/asia/pope-francis-rohingya.html', 'snippet': 'He met with Muslim refugees and heard their stories, but did not address his earlier public silence about them while in Myanmar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DHAKA, Bangladesh — On the eve of his return to Rome, Pope Francis on Friday used the word “Rohingya,” coming face-to-face with some of the persecuted Muslims whose plight had cast a long shadow over his visit to Myanmar and Bangladesh.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02POPE-01p/02pope1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02POPE-01p/02pope1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02POPE-01p/02pope1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02POPE-01p/02pope1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02POPE-01p/02pope1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02POPE-01p/02pope1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02POPE-01p/02pope1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘I Ask Forgiveness,’ Pope Francis Tells Rohingya Muslims in Bangladesh', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Presence of God Today Is Also Called Rohingya,’ Pope Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': "Cox's Bazar (Bangladesh)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dhaka (Bangladesh)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-01T17:43:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Horowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bc0b80a-410f-5dce-b592-066a7ddcfb99', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bc0b80a-410f-5dce-b592-066a7ddcfb99'}, {'abstract': '“8980: Book of Travelers,” a song cycle based on conversations the songwriter had on a nearly 9,000-mile Amtrak journey, comes to BAM.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/arts/music/gabriel-kahane-8980-book-of-travelers-review.html', 'snippet': '“8980: Book of Travelers,” a song cycle based on conversations the songwriter had on a nearly 9,000-mile Amtrak journey, comes to BAM.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day after Donald Trump was elected, the songwriter Gabriel Kahane decided to go on a listening tour: crisscrossing America by train and talking to as many people as he could. Leaving his cellphone and the internet behind, he spent two weeks and nearly 9,000 miles on Amtrak, collecting conversations and stories for what would become “8980: Book of Travelers,” a song cycle and solo concert — Mr. Kahane accompanying himself on piano — that had its premiere on Thursday night at the BAM Harvey Theater, where it continues through Saturday. A video backdrop, designed by Jim Findlay, showed landscapes, urban and rural, seen from trains in motion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/arts/music/02bamkahane1/02bamkahane1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/02/arts/music/02bamkahane1/02bamkahane1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/arts/music/02bamkahane1/02bamkahane1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/arts/music/02bamkahane1/02bamkahane1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/arts/music/02bamkaha