sty town in the northern Sinai Peninsula handed over three people accused of being Islamic State militants to Egyptian security forces. It was not the first time — they had handed over at least seven other people accused of being militants in the previous few months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02EGYPT-01/xxegypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02EGYPT-01/xxegypt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02EGYPT-01/xxegypt1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02EGYPT-01/xxegypt1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02EGYPT-01/xxegypt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02EGYPT-01/xxegypt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/world/02EGYPT-01/xxegypt1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Motives in Egypt’s Deadliest Terrorist Attack: Religion and Revenge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pondering Motives in Egypt’s Deadliest Terrorist Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sufism (Religion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bedouins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bir al-Abed (Egypt)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-01T23:31:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nour Youssef', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nour', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Youssef', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f460e897-c266-5548-89a0-a4ceb74fe64f', 'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f460e897-c266-5548-89a0-a4ceb74fe64f'}, {'abstract': 'The editor in chief of T Magazine explains how this issue’s cover story, featuring the rap luminary interviewed by Dean Baquet, came together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/insider/jay-z-dean-baquet-hanya-yanagihara.html', 'snippet': 'The editor in chief of T Magazine explains how this issue’s cover story, featuring the rap luminary interviewed by Dean Baquet, came together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T Magazine publishes 11 times a year, and the theme of each issue usually guides the content (at least to some degree): The Women’s Fashion issue is about women’s fashion; the Design issue is about design; the Travel issue is about … well, you get the idea.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/insider/03-insider-jayz/03-insider-jayz-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/insider/03-insider-jayz/03-insider-jayz-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/insider/03-insider-jayz/03-insider-jayz-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/insider/03-insider-jayz/03-insider-jayz-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 851, 'width': 1277, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/insider/03-insider-jayz/02-insider-jayz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/03/insider/03-insider-jayz/02-insider-jayz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/insider/03-insider-jayz/02-insider-jayz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Jay-Z Met Our Top Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jay-Z, Meet Dean Baquet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baquet, Dean', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-