 December 1967, an international tribunal said yes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/opinion/did-america-commit-war-crimes-in-vietnam.html', 'snippet': 'In December 1967, an international tribunal said yes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 1, 1967, the last day of the International War Crimes Tribunal’s second session, antiwar activists from around the world gathered in Roskilde, Denmark. The panel, also known as the Russell Tribunal after its founder, the philosopher Bertrand Russell, had spent a year investigating America’s intervention in Southeast Asia and was now ready to announce its findings. Tribunal members unanimously found the United States “guilty on all charges, including genocide, the use of forbidden weapons, maltreatment and killing of prisoners, violence and forceful movement of prisoners” in Vietnam and its neighbors Laos and Cambodia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/opinion/02vietnamfosterWeb/02vietnamfosterWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/02/opinion/02vietnamfosterWeb/02vietnamfosterWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/opinion/02vietnamfosterWeb/02vietnamfosterWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 548, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/opinion/02vietnamfosterWeb/02vietnamfosterWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1096, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/opinion/02vietnamfosterWeb/02vietnamfosterWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/02/opinion/02vietnamfosterWeb/02vietnamfosterWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/02/opinion/02vietnamfosterWeb/02vietnamfosterWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did America Commit War Crimes in Vietnam?', 'kicker': "Vietnam '67", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-02T03:18:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cody J. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cody', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Foster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a49e5e1d-75d8-5b3d-88a9-90b4f2492dcd', 'word_count': 1310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a49e5e1d-75d8-5b3d-88a9-90b4f2492dcd'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Jon Tester, Democrat of Montana, called it “Washington D.C. at its worst” as Republicans sought to speed through their amended bill, handwriting and all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/01/us/politics/hand-scribbled-tax-bill-outcry.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Jon Tester, Democrat of Montana, called it “Washington D.C. at its worst” as Republicans sought to speed through their amended bill, handwriting and all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — By midafternoon on Friday, Republicans had the votes to pass their tax bill in the Senate. What they did not have was a bill.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype