ns', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-02T19:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b207ad1-b5f9-517e-837c-6ae2e3242103', 'word_count': 683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b207ad1-b5f9-517e-837c-6ae2e3242103'}, {'abstract': 'Regenerative agriculture can help mitigate climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/02/opinion/sunday/soil-power-the-dirty-way-to-a-green-planet.html', 'snippet': 'Regenerative agriculture can help mitigate climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last great hope of avoiding catastrophic climate change may lie in a substance so commonplace that we typically ignore it or else walk all over it: the soil beneath our feet.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03leslie/03leslie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 572, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03leslie/03leslie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 572}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03leslie/03leslie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 976, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03leslie/03leslie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1764, 'width': 18