ch company and my husband is an engineer, so the industry is at the center of our lives. We have careers that allow us to help create products and tools our grandparents would never have thought were possible and to provide the kind of life for our family that they couldn’t have imagined. And it’s important to us to ensure that other people of color have a chance to contribute to the field and reap its benefits. With all those things on my mind, I left the conference energized and inspired by the ways in which tech is changing the world and the possibilities it holds for our community.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03bwilliams/03bwilliams-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03bwilliams/03bwilliams-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 482}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03bwilliams/03bwilliams-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03bwilliams/03bwilliams-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03bwilliams/03bwilliams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03bwilliams/03bwilliams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/opinion/sunday/03bwilliams/03bwilliams-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Intelligent’ Policing and My Innocent Children', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Will Tech Protect My Kids?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (Oakland, Calif)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-02T19:47:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bärí A. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bärí', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/15cdad97-de1c-56c4-96c6-b832352eff01', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15cdad97-de1c-56c4-96c6-b832352eff01'}, {'abstract': 'Spelman and Morehouse, the historically black colleges in Atlanta, are among a number of schools nationwide fielding complaints about sexual misconduct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/02/us/colleges-sexual-harassment.html', 'snippet': 'Spelman and Morehouse, the historically black colleges in Atlanta, are among a number of schools nationwide fielding complaints about sexual misconduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — The fliers appeared suddenly on a crisp morning in early November. They were scattered among golden leaves on the grounds of Spelman and Morehouse, the side-by-side women’s and men’s colleges that are two of the country’s most celebrated historically black schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/us/03colleges-01/00colleges-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/us/03colleges-01/00colleges-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/us/03colleges-01/00colleges-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/us/03colleges-01/00colleges-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/us/03colleges-01/00colleges-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/03/us/03colleges-01/00colleges-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'