ws a male speaker at a summit meeting of female political leaders in Iceland, the most gender-egalitarian country in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/02/world/europe/iceland-gender-equality-women-political-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'A Times reporter shadows a male speaker at a summit meeting of female political leaders in Iceland, the most gender-egalitarian country in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'REYKJAVIK, Iceland — Xavier Prats Monné could not say what exactly he expected from Iceland, this tiny gender utopia where selling pornography has been banned since 1869 and the world’s first openly lesbian prime minister was elected in 2009. But it was no shock that the driver who picked him up from the airport was a woman.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/world/europe/03Iceland/Iceland-slide-03XZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/world/europe/03Iceland/Iceland-slide-03XZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/world/europe/03Iceland/Iceland-slide-03XZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/world/europe/03Iceland/Iceland-slide-03XZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/world/europe/03Iceland/Iceland-slide-03XZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/03/world/europe/03Iceland/Iceland-slide-03XZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/world/europe/03Iceland/Iceland-slide-03XZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Man Among Female Leaders: ‘The Risk of Mansplaining Is Very High’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Meeting of Leaders, an Outnumbered Male', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'vis-dispatch', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prats Monne, Xavier', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-02T20:32:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3237188-275a-5750-9db0-9b705e28e0fe', 'word_count': 1423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3237188-275a-5750-9db0-9b705e28e0fe'}, {'abstract': 'The president has called claims of unusual contacts with Russia a “hoax.” But emails show top aides closely tracked Michael T. Flynn’s fateful call to the Russian ambassador.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/0