es, offices hold lavish parties, and people eat and drink till they are beyond sated. Not everyone, though. There is a grimmer corner of America. It is populated by men and, more commonly, women who shun food not because they are too poor to afford it, but because they are too troubled to desire it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Deadly Obsession, Food Is the Enemy', 'kicker': 'Retro Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANOREXIA NERVOSA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lenox Hill Hospital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Eating Disorders Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York-Presbyterian Hospital', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-03T23:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f022e72c-b7b7-5c5d-9197-7dcf71d1424e', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f022e72c-b7b7-5c5d-9197-7dcf71d1424e'}, {'abstract': '30 million people will suffer from eating disorders in their lifetime, yet decades after Karen Carpenter died from anorexia, myths about eating disorders continue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000005582329/myths-misperceptions-eating-disorders.html', 'snippet': '30 million people will suffer from eating disorders in their lifetime, yet decades after Karen Carpenter died from anorexia, my