], 'pub_date': '2017-12-04T03:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1667a65-95a1-5384-9dcd-9823742375c5', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1667a65-95a1-5384-9dcd-9823742375c5'}, {'abstract': 'Eugene is smart, but he’s uniquely unsuited for the moral dilemma that this week’s episode foists upon him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/03/arts/television/the-walking-dead-recap-time-for-after.html', 'snippet': 'Eugene is smart, but he’s uniquely unsuited for the moral dilemma that this week’s episode foists upon him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eugene is tremendously bright but lacks emotional intelligence — an easily exploited combo. A majestically mulleted survivor, he speaks in a florid manner somewhere between professorial and Twain-like, talking circles around gruffer, terser company. He’s demonstrated a shrewd skill for preservation, both of himself and of the group, a talent that went unappreciated among the militia and motivated his defection to the Saviors. Early in this week’s episode, Negan doles out a rare morsel of praise for Eugene’s beautiful brain, offering the precious gift of a handshake as a token of respect. “This place is about pooling and organizing strength,” he tells Eugene, implicitly placing him within the trusted inner circle. Eugene is manipulated with surprising ease for someone so clearly smart, eagerly snapping up the first scrap of praise tossed his way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/watching/03walkingdead03/03walkingdead03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/03/watching/03walkingdead03/03walkingdead03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/watching/03walkingdead03/03walkingdead03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/watching/03walkingdead03/03walkingdead03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/watching/03walkingdead03/03walkingdead03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/03/watching/03walkingdead03/03walkingdead03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/03/watching/03walkingdead03/03walkingdead03-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Walking Dead’ Season 8, Episode 7: Pyrrhic Victories', 'kicker': 'The Walking Dead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Walking Dead (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-04T03:04:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Bramesco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middle