ducation (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-06T08:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Proulx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Proulx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0bdfc80-09de-51aa-b449-1b341cb96b98', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0bdfc80-09de-51aa-b449-1b341cb96b98'}, {'abstract': 'Our co-chief film critic hopes that sexual harassment scandals will make a difference. But she knows that bias against women is systemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/06/movies/2017-was-a-year-of-reckoning-in-hollywood-will-2018-be-the-year-of-change.html', 'snippet': 'Our co-chief film critic hopes that sexual harassment scandals will make a difference. But she knows that bias against women is systemic.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Do you think this will change things?” More than one person has asked me that question over the past few months. What they — what so many of us — want to know is whether the allegations of sexual abuse and harassment against some of the biggest men in the entertainment industry will have lasting repercussions. Invariably, I say yes, though with hesitation. I yearn to believe that both these accusations and the anger that’s surged in their wake will make a difference. But I wonder how this anger can be directed to effect real change, specifically in an institution that’s been as historically rigged against women as the American movie industry. Because anger alone isn’t enough.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/arts/10best-films-weinstein/10best-films-weinstein-articleLarge.jpg', 'hei