ide to the (very) many versions of Handel’s oratorio strewn over the New York music scene each December and how they grew.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How do you distinguish among the host of performances of Handel’s “Messiah” that crowd New York’s musical calendar each December? Some have choruses of a dozen or so; some field hundreds. Some use baroque instruments; some, modern. Some (a lot) are amateur; some are professionals. Some leave the singing to the people on stage; some (heaven help us) let the audience-cum-congregation participate. Some offer a comfortable holiday tradition; some (we’re looking at you, Trinity Wall Street) offer something closer to a sacred rite.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08messiah-1/08messiah-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08messiah-1/08messiah-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08messiah-1/08messiah-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08messiah-1/08messiah-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08messiah-1/08messiah-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08messiah-1/08messiah-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'