, Nathan Farb, a left-leaning Jewish artist, was chosen by the government to represent the United States on a public relations trip to the Soviet Union, where he took portraits of Novosibirsk citizens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to believe, but in 1977, the United States government tapped Nathan Farb, a left-leaning, hippie, Jewish artist to represent America on a public relations trip to the Soviet Union. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Soviets, They’re Not So Different From Us', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nathan Farb', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farb, Nathan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Romanian Communist Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-07T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blaustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blaustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a757bfde-a329-55ff-b934-68128294a323', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a757bfde-a329-55ff-b934-68128294a323'}, {'abstract': 'A.O. Scott, co-chief film critic for The Times, and Wesley Morris, critic at large, discuss the 10 great movie performances of 2017.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/vi