umbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08tovey2/09tovey2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/08/arts/08tovey2/09tovey2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Out, Out and Away! Russell Tovey on Playing a Gay Superhero', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out, Out and Away! Playing a Gay Superhero', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Freedom Fighters: The Ray (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tovey, Russell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Seed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Television Network', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-07T18:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93494046-9db7-56f8-971f-0c643329b36b', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93494046-9db7-56f8-971f-0c643329b36b'}, {'abstract': 'These beautifully illustrated chapter books for brand new readers are very short — and very, very good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/07/books/review/new-reader-early-chapter.html', 'snippet': 'These beautifully illustrated chapter books for brand new readers are very short — and very, very good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My favorite books for fledgling readers don’t have ranked letters or numbers or other indicators of “levels” on the covers. They’re not part of megaseries like The Magic Treehouse or Junie B. Jones (useful as those books can be to get readers going). What they have in common is gorgeous art and extremely simple but highly literary writing — the kind of writing that lets a young reader know what an inner life can sound like. And while they couldn’t really be called full-fledged chapter books, they are often cleverly divided into a few very short chapters, as a sort of secret handshake. These books tell new readers they have fully embarked on the journey to independent reading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/books/review/21MariasPicks/21MariasPicks-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/21/books/review/21MariasPicks/21MariasPicks-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/books/review/21MariasPicks/21MariasPicks-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/books/review/21MariasPicks/21MariasPicks-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/books/review/21MariasPicks/21MariasPicks-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'