', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dianna writes: My partner, Nick, eats leftovers straight from the fridge (pizza, Chinese food, sometimes a thing he calls a “cold cheese roll up”). I’m sensitive to the smell of cold foods. I can be sitting in a different room when he opens the fridge, and it still turns my stomach. Please tell him to stop.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/magazine/10mag-hodgman/10mag-10hodgman-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/10/magazine/10mag-hodgman/10mag-10hodgman-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 589}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/magazine/10mag-hodgman/10mag-10hodgman-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1005, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/magazine/10mag-hodgman/10mag-10hodgman-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 1260, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/magazine/10mag-hodgman/10mag-10hodgman-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/10/magazine/10mag-hodgman/10mag-10hodgman-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/magazine/10mag-hodgman/10mag-10hodgman-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name