r. Trump has yet to bend the presidency to his will, he is at least wrestling it to a draw.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/09/us/politics/donald-trump-president.html', 'snippet': 'With Twitter as his Excalibur, the president takes on his doubters, powered by long spells of cable news and a dozen Diet Cokes. But if Mr. Trump has yet to bend the presidency to his will, he is at least wrestling it to a draw.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Around 5:30 each morning, President Trump wakes and tunes into the television in the White House’s master bedroom. He flips to CNN for news, moves to “Fox & Friends” for comfort and messaging ideas, and sometimes watches MSNBC’s “Morning Joe” because, friends suspect, it fires him up for the day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/us/politics/10dc-trumpopus-top/12dc-trumpday-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/10/us/politics/10dc-trumpopus-top/12dc-trumpday-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/us/politics/10dc-trumpopus-top/12dc-trumpday-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 818, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/us/politics/10dc-trumpopus-top/12dc-trumpday-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1637, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/10/us/politics/10dc-trumpopus-top/12dc-trumpday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c