s', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/97c67e2e-2fc5-542f-87ea-2db50f0f584d', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97c67e2e-2fc5-542f-87ea-2db50f0f584d'}, {'abstract': 'The Oscar-winning actor concentrates on subtle acting in his new production of “Falstaff” at Opera Vlaanderen in Belgium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/11/arts/music/christoph-waltz-verdi-falstaff.html', 'snippet': 'The Oscar-winning actor concentrates on subtle acting in his new production of “Falstaff” at Opera Vlaanderen in Belgium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANTWERP, Belgium — Christoph Waltz acts musically — even operatically. Characters like the cunning S.S. officer he played in Quentin Tarantino’s film “Inglourious Basterds,” for which he won the first of two Oscars, and the sybaritic profiteer in the coming “Downsizing” draw much of their sly charisma from Mr. Waltz’s artful flow and pacing, and his command of vocal shades from soft purr to sharp steel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/arts/12WALTZ1/12WALTZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/12/arts/12WALTZ1/12WALTZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/arts/12WALTZ1/12WALTZ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/arts/12WALTZ1/12WALTZ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': '