'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-11T23:48:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e702767-ef03-56ac-a9a8-51376a8e86ee', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e702767-ef03-56ac-a9a8-51376a8e86ee'}, {'abstract': 'Shortly before a unanimous vote, the education policy board introduced a proposal for children with disabilities to get a diploma without passing state exams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/11/nyregion/regents-graduation-disabled-students.html', 'snippet': 'Shortly before a unanimous vote, the education policy board introduced a proposal for children with disabilities to get a diploma without passing state exams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York State Board of Regents went further on Monday in its efforts to make it easier for students with disabilities to graduate from high school, essentially eliminating the requirement that they pass any Regents exams.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regents Make Graduation Easier for Disabled Students', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Makes Graduation Easier for Disabled Students', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Regents (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-11T23:51:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1826d0df-994f-5d63-a7c3-a237cbed2aea', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1826d0df-994f-5d63-a7c3-a237cbed2aea'}, {'abstract': 'A Treasury report on tax cuts that’s a sick joke, but very much in the modern G.O.P. tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/11/opinion/mnuchin-paul-ryan-taxes.html', 'snippet': 'A Treasury report on tax cuts that’s a sick joke, but very much in the modern G.O.P. tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday the Treasury Department released a one-page report claiming that tax cuts would pay for themselves. The document was a shameless attempt to fool the public — carefully worded to imply that economic experts at Treasury (they’re still in there somewhere, maybe locked in a closet) had actually done an analysis to that effect, without explicitly saying so. In fact, there was no economic analysis; Trump officials just made up numbers that would give them the result they wanted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12KRUGMAN/12KRUGMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12KRUGMAN/12KRUGMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12KRUGMAN/12KRUGMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12KRUGMAN/12KRUGMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1380, 'wi