url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/11/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-in-the-face-of-new-dangers-doubling-down-on-daily-life.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, December 12, 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We cannot stop living. There was the event on the bike path last month. I tell you, I’m more concerned by the derailment on this line last summer.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: In the Face of New Dangers, Doubling Down on Daily Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-12-12T02:15:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/a489dd41-f497-597b-9de1-0c9e598ff304', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a489dd41-f497-597b-9de1-0c9e598ff304'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s radicalism is unusual. For starters, we have radical anger without radical policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/11/opinion/radicalism-trump-moore.html', 'snippet': 'Today’s radicalism is unusual. For starters, we have radical anger without radical policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a striking moment in the focus group that consultant Frank Luntz recently held with a group of Roy Moore supporters in Alabama. One of the voters said that the women who are accusing Moore of harassment are being paid to do so. Luntz asked the group how many people thought the women are being paid. A bunch of hands shot up and voices called out that all of the women are being paid.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Wrong With Radicalism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s  Wrong With Radicalism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luntz, Frank I', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-12T02:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d6b2c2e-1161-5cfc-94fd-272e9f167f87', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d6b2c2e-1161-5cfc-94fd-272e9f167f87'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Tuesday, December 12, 2017.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/11/pageoneplus/corrections-december-12-2017.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Tuesday, December 12, 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: December 12, 2017', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-12-12T02:35:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5d2ab8f-0393-549f-bbac-8f791aeb106d', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5d2ab8f-0393-549f-bbac-8f791aeb106d'}, {'abstract': 'The choice lines and the soundtrack hits are there in this enjoyable adaptation of the movie. Now it’s time to make a full-fledged show out of a quasi concert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/11/theater/review-in-this-cruel-intentions-high-school-schemers-sing-the-best-of-the-90s.html', 'snippet': 'The choice lines and the soundtrack hits are there in this enjoyable adaptation of the movie. Now it’s time to make a full-fledged show out of a quasi concert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no “Clueless,” but “Cruel Intentions” has endured better than most 1990s teen movies. Partly this has to do with its cast, especially Reese Witherspoon, just as good playing saintly as she would be ruthless in “Election” a couple of months later. But what really made Roger Kumble’s film stand out were the timeless structure and timely embroideries: a fail-safe plot based on the 18th-century novel “Les Liaisons Dangereuses” combined with an arch ’90s sensibility and an inspired soundtrack — the denouement, set to the Verve’s “Bitter Sweet Symphony,” was worthy of Scorsese.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/14/arts/14CRUEL-INTENTIONS/12CRUEL-INTENTIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/14/arts/14CRUEL-INTENTIONS/12CRUEL-INTENTIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/14/arts/14CRUEL-INTENTIONS/12CRUEL-INTENTIONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/14/arts/14CRUEL-INTENTIONS/12CRUEL-INTENTIONS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/14/arts/14CRUEL-INTENTIONS/12CRUEL-INTENTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/14/arts/14CRUEL-INTENTIONS/12CRUEL-INTENTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/14/arts/14CRUEL-INTENTIONS/12CRUEL-INTENTIONS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rev