alue': 'Sessions, Jefferson B III', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bentley, Robert J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strange, Luther', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ivey, Kay', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Morris Jackson', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-12T18:11:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74486845-6fd9-5b9b-9bc0-b302ee07d557', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74486845-6fd9-5b9b-9bc0-b302ee07d557'}, {'abstract': 'Danny Mena and Oscar León Bernal of Hecho en Dumbo return to Brooklyn, and other restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/12/dining/brooklyn-cider-house-nyc-restaurant-news.html', 'snippet': 'Danny Mena and Oscar León Bernal of Hecho en Dumbo return to Brooklyn, and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BROOKLYN CIDER HOUSE Peter Yi, who founded PJ Wine in Inwood, has moved on to hard cider. He already makes five styles in the Hudson Valley (some from apples grown in his orchards). But now he is increasing his production, adding this spacious new cider house, bar and restaurant, with fermenting containers and aging barrels and tanks, in Bushwick, Brooklyn. Inspired by cider traditions in the Basque Country, he will tap some of the ciders being served directly from the barrels and tanks, as they do in Spain. The menu will have a Basque influence, with chorizo simmered in cider, an omelet with salted cod, Spanish cheeses and cured meats, and slabs of beef. “I want to make cider that will change people’s assumption that wine goes best with food,” he said. “Just like what happened to me.” His partners include his sister, Susan Yi. The industrial space, warmed with plenty of wood, has three dining areas and communal tables. The ciders will also be sold for takeout. (Opens Thursday): 1100 Flushing Avenue (Varick Avenue), Bushwick, Brooklyn, 347-295-0308, brooklynciderhouse.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/13/dining/13OFF-sub/merlin_131156897_364aacd9-8f13-4e9b-8fbb-49bb3e5f758a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/13/dining/13OFF-sub/merlin_131156897_364aacd9-8f13-4e9b-8fbb-49bb3e5f758a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/13/dining/13OFF-sub/merlin_131156897_364aacd9-8f13-4e9b-8fbb-49bb3e5f758a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/13/dining/13OFF-sub/merlin_131156897_364aacd9-8f13-4e9b-8fbb-49bb3e5f758a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/13/dining/13OFF-sub/13OFF-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/13/dining/13OFF-sub/13OFF-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/13/dining/13OFF-sub/13OFF-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Cider House Opens in Bushwick', 'kicker': 'Off the Menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Cider House (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Essex Street Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saison (San Francisco, Calif, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-12T18:18:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c385fa1b-a808-55fe-91e3-7dac23ac1509', 'word_count': 1053, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c385fa1b-a808-55fe-91e3-7dac23ac1509'}, {'abstract': 'Globally, we throw out about a third of all food. That matters a lot in the fight against hunger, but reducing waste could also help cut greenhouse gas emissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/12/climate/food-waste-emissions.html', 'snippet': 'Globally, we throw out about a third of all food. That matters a lot in the fight against hunger, but reducing waste could also help cut greenhouse gas emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That’s important for at least two reasons. The less the world wastes, the easier it will be to meet the food needs of the global population in coming years. Second, cutting back on waste could go a long way to reducing greenhouse gas emissions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/12cli-foodwaste/12cli-foodwaste-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/12cli-foodwaste/12cli-foodwaste-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/12cli-foodwaste/12cli-foodwaste-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/12cli-foodwaste/12cli-foodwaste-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/12cli-foodwaste/12cli-foodwaste-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/12cli-foodwaste/12cli-foodwaste-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/12cli-foodwaste/12cli-foodwaste-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Much Food Do We Waste? Probably More Than You Think', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Climate Change (Album)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-12T18:28:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_na