A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Doug (1954- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-13T04:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/58567c98-7c71-5d22-93b4-a3de0a30810b', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58567c98-7c71-5d22-93b4-a3de0a30810b'}, {'abstract': 'Doug Jones strikes a blow against Donald Trump and for morality in American politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/12/opinion/roy-moore-loss-alabama.html', 'snippet': 'Doug Jones strikes a blow against Donald Trump and for morality in American politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Alabama’s voters chose Doug Jones for the United States Senate is cause for celebration. A triumph for decency and common sense in a state that seemed for a time at risk of abandoning both, Mr. Jones’s win narrows the Republicans’ Senate majority and delivers a deeply deserved rebuke to President Trump. It is hard to get too intoxicated by a slim victory over an atrocious candidate, a suspected sexual abuser with bigoted politics, but Alabama, the Senate and the nation will be a whole lot better off with Mr. Jones than with Roy Moore.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/14/opinion/13edSub/13edSub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subTyp