g-activities-for-jay-z-and-dean-baquet-in-conversation.html', 'snippet': 'What does Jay-Z reveal about therapy, marriage and politics in this Times interview?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before reading the article: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching Activities for: ‘Jay-Z and Dean Baquet, in Conversation’', 'kicker': 'Article of the Day', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-12-14T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Crosson Gilpin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': 'Crosson', 'lastname': 'Gilpin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b178eba6-34e6-55e2-8ec1-16d3e77f350f', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b178eba6-34e6-55e2-8ec1-16d3e77f350f'}, {'abstract': 'All the major battles for equal rights — racial, ethnic, gender, sexual orientation, disability — are explored in “The Good Fight.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/a-look-at-the-heart-wrenching-moments-from-equal-rights-battles/', 'snippet': 'All the major battles for equal rights — racial, ethnic, gender, sexual orientation, disability — are explored in “The Good Fight.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 54-mile march for voting rights from Selma to Alabama’s state capital, Montgomery, took more than good legs and sturdy shoes. It took defying the police, who ambushed hundreds of men, women and children — on a bridge named for a Klu Klux Klan leader — and beat them bloody. It took a court order and it took journalists covering the struggles to tell and shock the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look at the Heart-Wrenching Moments From Equal Rights Battles', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Social Responsibility', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-14T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn Nieves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nieves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/465e1438-01ed-5226-8ee1-4536b9370b4d', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/465e1438-01ed-5226-8ee1-4536b9370b4d'}, {'abstract': 'An import that seems more authentic in its overseas market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-indian-butterscotch-ice-cream.html', 'snippet': 'An import that seems more authentic in its overseas market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travelers in India who are not searching for themselves often instead come searching for culinary transcendence. The possible food quests are endless, something I’ve learned over the course of repeat reporting trips to the country, and I visited Delhi in October with an agenda of my own. I looked forward to local delicacies, like chhole bhature, a fried-bread-and-chickpea breakfast, and daulat ki chaat, sweetened milk froth with pistachios and cardamon. But there was one food I anticipated more than any other, a taste I had been craving since I first visited India a year before. It was then, on an impossibly humid day in Bangalore, that I sought relief in the freezer box of a local shop and found that is was full of butterscotch ice cream cones.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-lor/17mag-17lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-lor/17mag-17lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-lor/17mag-17lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-lor/17mag-17lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-lor/17mag-lor-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-lor/17mag-lor-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-lor/17mag-lor-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Indian Butterscotch Ice Cream', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Butterscotch Ice Cream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-14T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Crair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crair', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/819fb1d8-b4b8-51b2-8f46-aa241464f1d7', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/819fb1d8-b4b8-51b2-8f46-aa241464f1d7'}, {'abstract': 'Years of obsession have resulted in a legendary dessert', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/magazine/secrets-russian-honey-cake-michelle-polzine.html', 'snippet': 'Years of obsession have resulted in a legendary dessert', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Michelle Polzine opened 20th Century Cafe, a tiny pastry shop in San Francisco in 2013, her majestic Russian honey cake enchanted sweet tooths everywhere. Food writers and pastry chefs flew in from across the country to marvel at the gravity-defying stack of airy cake layers slathered with glossy honey-cream frosting. With just two components, the cake seems simple, but those components unite to release a wave of malty, bittersweet and delightfully tangy notes with each bite.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/magazine/17mag-eat1-copy/17mag-17eat-t_CA0-articleLa