a-same-sex-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'The move by lawmakers to allow only domestic partnerships in the self-governing British territory reverses a court ruling from May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — At a time when support for same-sex marriage seems to be slowly advancing in some parts of the world, legislators in Bermuda have restored a ban on the unions, just six months after the island’s highest court approved them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bermuda Legalized Same-Sex Marriage 6 Months Ago. Now, It’s Going to Be Banned.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '6 Months In, Gay Marriage Is Reversed In Bermuda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bermuda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-14T11:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/999947ae-7f02-572c-b813-d4bcabdcdd5c', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/999947ae-7f02-572c-b813-d4bcabdcdd5c'}, {'abstract': 'This psycho-in-the-woods tale benefits from sensitive writing and organic performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/movies/desolation-review.html', 'snippet': 'This psycho-in-the-woods tale benefits from sensitive writing and organic performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Working a low body count and a slow burn, “Desolation” is a decent short film that’s been unwisely expanded to feature length. A psycho-in-the-woods tale whose villain is more funny-looking than alarming, this debut effort from the director Sam Patton is notable mainly for the beautifully organic performances of its two female leads. In tandem with Matt Anderson and Michael Larson-Kangas’s surprisingly sensitive script, the women create a believably intimate bond between their beleaguered characters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/movies/desolation1/merlin_131167364_2943965d-db34-498a-94a5-1884875363ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/12/movies/desolation1/merlin_131167364_2943965d-db34-498a-94a5-1884875363ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/movies/desolation1/merlin_131167364_2943965d-db34-498a-94a5-1884875363ad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/movies/desolation1/merlin_131167364_2943965d-db34-498a-94a5-1884875363ad-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/movies/desolation1/desolation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/12/movies/desolation1/desolation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/movies/desolation1/desolation1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Emotional ‘Desolation’ and Woodland Horror', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desolation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Desolation (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patton, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-14T12:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a880306-8f86-593c-a454-e43cc5352d92', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a880306-8f86-593c-a454-e43cc5352d92'}, {'abstract': 'In this droll comedy from Pavan Moondi, a pair of feckless layabouts are assigned to video-record a wedding at a Mexican resort. Mishaps ensue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/movies/sundowners-review.html', 'snippet': 'In this droll comedy from Pavan Moondi, a pair of feckless layabouts are assigned to video-record a wedding at a Mexican resort. Mishaps ensue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A familiar comedy subgenre — that of hapless protagonists having misadventures at a wedding gathering at an exotic resort (see: “Forgetting Sarah Marshall” and “Mike and Dave Need Wedding Dates”) — is given a low-key workout in “Sundowners,” a Canadian indie seeking to subvert expectations but