nces return to the Ailey repertory: “Shelter,” a potent statement about homelessness, and the rambunctious “Stack-Up.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/arts/dance/alvin-ailey-shelter-stack-up.html', 'snippet': 'Two 1980s dances return to the Ailey repertory: “Shelter,” a potent statement about homelessness, and the rambunctious “Stack-Up.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two productions from the 1980s returned to the repertory of the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater this week, in refurbished form. The new iterations of Jawole Willa Jo Zollar’s “Shelter” (1988) and Talley Beatty’s “Stack-Up” (1982), part of the company’s five-week City Center season, proved a study in contrasts of how dances can weather the passage of time. While “Shelter,” a potent statement on homelessness and displacement, speaks pointedly to the present, the rambunctious “Stack-Up” seems bound to another era, which made it no less intriguing to watch.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/arts/18SHELTER-2/15tesseract-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/18/arts/18SHELTER-2/15tesseract-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/arts/18SHELTER-2/15tesseract-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/arts/18SHELTER-2/15tesseract-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1509, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images