a Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b93ba1b-3a74-5348-9a55-c0a4f1fef10f', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b93ba1b-3a74-5348-9a55-c0a4f1fef10f'}, {'abstract': 'Pittsburgh has a shot at clinching home-field advantage in the playoffs. Big games in the A.F.C. West and N.F.C. West could help decide those divisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/sports/nfl-picks-predictions-week-15.html', 'snippet': 'Pittsburgh has a shot at clinching home-field advantage in the playoffs. Big games in the A.F.C. West and N.F.C. West could help decide those divisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are only two N.F.L. games in Week 15 between teams that The Upshot’s Playoff Simulator gives a 50 percent chance or greater of making the playoffs, but there are three crucial matchups. The Chiefs and the Chargers will meet in a game that could decide the A.F.C. West, the Rams and the Seahawks will battle for the N.F.C. West, and a Sunday afternoon matchup between the Steelers and the Patriots could clinch home-field advantage throughout the playoffs for Pittsburgh (with some help from Houston). Here are our picks against the spread.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/sports/17nflpreview-steelers/17nflpreview-steelers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/17/sports/17nflpreview-steelers/17nflpreview-steelers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/sports/17nflpreview-steelers/17nflpreview-steelers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/sports/17nflpreview-steelers/17nflpreview-steelers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/sports/17nflpreview-steelers/17nflpreview-steelers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/17/sports/17nflpreview-steelers/17nflpreview-steelers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/sports/17nflpreview-steelers/17nflpreview-steelers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Picks Week 15: Steelers and Patriots Battle for A.F.C. Superiority', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steelers and Patriots Battle for A.F.C. Superiority', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Chargers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-14T19:41:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7c579ea-6f6f-5aaf-af53-b346aa5b5aee', 'word_count': 2389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7c579ea-6f6f-5aaf-af53-b346aa5b5aee'}, {'abstract': 'For the Amsterdam museum, which he visited often as a teenager, the architect oversaw the mounting of 700 artworks by the likes of Jeff Koons and Kazimir Malevich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/14/arts/design/rem-koolhaas-stedelijk-amsterdam.html', 'snippet': 'For the Amsterdam museum, which he visited often as a teenager, the architect oversaw the mounting of 700 artworks by the likes of Jeff Koons and Kazimir Malevich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMSTERDAM — The renowned Dutch architect Rem Koolhaas has designed landmark buildings in cities from Miami Beach to Beijing, so it would be natural for him to delegate the task of rehanging a local museum’s collection. But because the museum in question is the Stedelijk in Amsterdam, which Mr. Koolhaas visited regularly in his youth, he took a very personal interest.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/16/arts/16arts-print/merlin_127558796_494253d8-0ab6-48a6-9d7c-e2fba9ac4b65-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/16/arts/16arts-print/merlin_127558796_494253d8-0ab6-48a6-9d7c-e2fba9ac4b65-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/16/arts/16arts-print/merlin_127558796_494253d8-0ab6-48a6-9d7c-e2fba9ac4b65-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': '