 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/582cc8b5-baf7-5d77-acd4-c5af18a449c9'}, {'abstract': 'Many people love long car trips. For my girlfriend and me, they’re full of danger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/16/opinion/sunday/the-risks-of-traveling-while-queer.html', 'snippet': 'Many people love long car trips. For my girlfriend and me, they’re full of danger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you get excited at the thought of packing up the car and heading home for the holidays or setting off on a cross-country road trip? I don’t.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17spataro/17spataro-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17spataro/17spataro-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17spataro/17spataro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17spataro/17spataro-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1181, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17spataro/17spataro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17spataro/17spataro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17spataro/17spataro-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Risks of Traveling While Queer', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Traveling While Queer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-16T19:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Spataro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spataro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dd60d48-cdc7-55d3-b9c1-54cdebf9550f', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dd60d48-cdc7-55d3-b9c1-54cdebf9550f'}, {'abstract': 'Sexual consent can be more complicated than a one-word answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/16/sunday-review/when-saying-yes-is-easier-than-saying-no.html', 'snippet': 'Sexual consent can be more complicated than a one-word answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, my female friends and I have spoken, with knowing nods, about a sexual interaction we call “the place of no return.” It is a kind of sexual nuance that most women instinctively understand: the situation you thought you wanted, or maybe you actually never wanted, but somehow here you are and it’s happening and you desperately want out, but you know that at this point exiting the situation would be more difficult than simply lying there and waiting for it to be over. In other words: saying yes when we really mean no.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17bennett/17bennett-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17bennett/17bennett-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 566}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17bennett/17bennett-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 966, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17bennett/17bennett-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 1459, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17bennett/17bennett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17bennett/17bennett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17bennett/17bennett-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Saying ‘Yes’ Is Easier Than Saying ‘No’', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When ‘Yes’ Is Easier Than ‘No’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roupenian, Kristen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-16T19:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Bennett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2a1674f-6a02-5c75-96b6-f753c237473b', 'word_count': 1146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2a1674f-6a02-5c75-96b6-f753c237473b'}, {'abstract': 'It would be a healthy sign that we, as a civilization, are still planning a future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/16/opinion/sunday/lets-go-to-mars.html', 'snippet': 'It would be a healthy sign that we, as a civilization, are still planning a future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The issues Donald Trump and I can find to agree on are few. I know this makes us both sad. Some people mock him for gorging himself on multiple Big Macs and Filets-o-Fish, but this is actually my favorite thing about him. I understand he likes elephants. And as of Monday, it turns out we agree on a third thing: sending human beings back to the moon, and to Mars.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17krieder/17krieder-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/17/opinion/sunday/17krieder/17krieder-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 