ain, moved into a corner storefront, it covered up a glass mosaic. Word of the mural’s absence spread quickly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The glass mosaic had been a familiar sight on the southeast corner of 125th Street and Frederick Douglass Boulevard in Harlem for more than a decade. But that changed last month when workers for a sneaker store that had moved into the storefront on that corner began installing a new facade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/nyregion/18mural1/merlin_131273021_ac841ea3-784b-4fa4-a4c7-8c1b70f95185-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/18/nyregion/18mural1/merlin_131273021_ac841ea3-784b-4fa4-a4c7-8c1b70f95185-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/nyregion/18mural1/merlin_131273021_ac841ea3-784b-4fa4-a4c7-8c1b70f95185-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/nyregion/18mural1/merlin_131273021_ac841ea3-784b-4fa4-a4c7-8c1b70f95185-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/nyregion/18mural1/00mural1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/18/nyregion/18mural1/00mural1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'