e/11845226-89df-5e29-a65f-6b9812f60bdc', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11845226-89df-5e29-a65f-6b9812f60bdc'}, {'abstract': 'A group supported by The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund helps those who fled the devastation to start a new life in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/17/opinion/helping-refugees-puerto-rico.html', 'snippet': 'A group supported by The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund helps those who fled the devastation to start a new life in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like millions of others in Puerto Rico, Enid Rosa had her normal life washed away in September by Hurricane Maria. Her house in Rincón, a coastal city on the western edge of the island, was inundated. Outside, the flooding was even worse. “It was really bad,” Ms. Rosa said. “But it was scarier after the hurricane: No food. No water. All our basic utilities lost. It was really after the fact that it got scary.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/opinion/18mon3web/18wed3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/18/opinion/18mon3web/18wed3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/opinion/18mon3web/18wed3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/opinion/18mon3web/18wed3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/18/opini