': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcc051b9-ae79-5406-a820-3fc8960a81fd', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcc051b9-ae79-5406-a820-3fc8960a81fd'}, {'abstract': 'Starting in 2007, the Advanced Aerospace Threat Identification Program analyzed unidentified airborne objects. Two months ago, The Times found out about it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/18/insider/secret-pentagon-ufo-program.html', 'snippet': 'Starting in 2007, the Advanced Aerospace Threat Identification Program analyzed unidentified airborne objects. Two months ago, The Times found out about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our readers are plenty interested in unidentified flying objects. We know that from the huge response to our front-page Sunday article (published online just after noon on Saturday) revealing a secret Pentagon program to investigate U.F.O.s. The piece, by the Pentagon correspondent Helene Cooper, the author Leslie Kean and myself — a contributor to The Times after a 45-year staff career — has dominated the most emailed and most viewed lists since.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/autossell/STILL2/STILL2-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/19/autossell/STILL2/STILL2-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/autossell/STILL2/STILL2-jumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 427, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/autossell/STILL2/STILL2-superJumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 427, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/autossell/STILL2/STILL2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/19/autossell/STILL2/STILL2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/autossell/STILL2/STILL2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Trail of a Secret Pentagon U.F.O. Program', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.F.O.s, the Pentagon and The Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unidentified Flying Objects (UFO)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-18T23:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ralph Blumenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ralph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blumenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/accb531f-29eb-5860-b3b6-77f964307d6d', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/accb531f-29eb-5860-b3b6-77f964307d6d'}, {'abstract': 'Brad Thomas Parsons’s “Distillery Cats” profiles the felines who patrol the world’s great distilleries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/18/dining/drinks/distillery-cats-book-brad-thomas-parsons.html', 'snippet': 'Brad Thomas Parsons’s “Distillery Cats” profiles the felines who patrol the world’s great distilleries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As mousers, cats earn their keep guarding the sacks of grain that are essential to distilleries and breweries. The author Brad Thomas Parsons, a cat person, has documented 30 of these felines, giving their names, habits and locations, with charmingly sketched portraits by Julia Kuo. Alongside are some cocktail recipes, including the Idle Revolver, made with whiskey, coffee liqueur and orange bitters. Stuff it into a stocking or give it with a bottle of whiskey: “Distillery Cats: Profiles in Courage of the World’s Most Spirited Mousers” by Brad Thomas Parsons (Ten Speed Press, $14.99).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burnerbook/20burnerbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burnerbook/20burnerbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 811}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burnerbook/20burnerbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burnerbook/20burnerbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1515, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo'