ion in the region over President Trump’s decision to recognize Jerusalem as Israel’s capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/18/us/politics/pence-middle-east-tax-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The decision also came amid mounting tension in the region over President Trump’s decision to recognize Jerusalem as Israel’s capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Vice President Mike Pence is pushing back his long-planned trip to the Middle East, his office confirmed Monday, citing the vote on the tax overhaul legislation this week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/us/politics/19dc-pence/merlin_131216219_c2f3553b-4d65-455c-873a-b6260b3afc62-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/19/us/politics/19dc-pence/merlin_131216219_c2f3553b-4d65-455c-873a-b6260b3afc62-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/us/politics/19dc-pence/merlin_131216219_c2f3553b-4d65-455c-873a-b6260b3afc62-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/us/politics/19dc-pence/merlin_131216219_c2f3553b-4d65-455c-873a-b6260b3afc62-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/us/politics/19dc-pence/19dc-pence-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/19/us/politics/19dc-pence/19dc-pence-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/19/us/politics/19dc-pence/19dc-pence-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pence Postpones Trip to Middle East, Citing Vote on Tax Bill This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pence Postpones Middle East Trip, Citing Vote on Tax Bill, Not Mounting Tensions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-18T23:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tackett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tackett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49a821dd-de4c-5eb5-a3bc-64065b3c6655', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49a821dd-de4c-5eb5-a3bc-64065b3c6655'}, {'abstract': 'A kitchen centrifuge from Dave Arnold can distill the essence of common ingredients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/18/dining/spinzall-centrifuge-dave-arnold.html', 'snippet': 'A kitchen centrifuge from Dave Arnold can distill the essence of common ingredients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For that cook who is inspired more by Nathan Myhrvold than Julia Child, there is the Spinzall, a centrifuge that can clarify liquids like flavored oils, juices and spirits. It was developed by Dave Arnold — the bar geek — to be more compact and cheaper than industrial models, yet more powerful and with a larger capacity than the small ones now available. It can process a half-liter (about 17 ounces) at a time to separate peeled, chopped tomatoes into tomato water and tomato paste; and spin diced bananas mixed with rum into clear banana-flavored rum. For home cooks, it’s an expensive toy that is not likely to displace the food processor, but chefs and bartenders may want one under the tree: Spinzall, $799, amazon.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burner-spin/20burner-spin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burner-spin/20burner-spin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burner-spin/20burner-spin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burner-spin/20burner-spin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burner-spin/20burner-spin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burner-spin/20burner-spin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20burner-spin/20burner-spin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gadget for the Cook Who Has Everything', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Whirl: Just the Gadget to Send Some Cooks Into a Tizzy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arnold, David (Author)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-18T23:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b45fa90-5737-552e-9b1b-3caf642acc93', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b45fa90-5737-552e-9b1b-3caf642acc93'}, {'abstract': 'Financial firms would see a larger tax cut than manufacturers, a University of Pennsylvania study concluded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/18/us/politics/republican-tax-cuts-industries-.html', 'snippet': 'Financial firms would see a larger tax cut than manufacturers, a University of Pennsylvania study concluded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The $1.5 trillion tax bill heading for a vote this week is a big win for corporations overall. But not every business benefits equally, with bigger cuts flowing to financial firms and the real estate industry than to manufacturers or mining companies, a new economic analysis finds.', '