36cf795d72c3'}, {'abstract': 'The human rights lawyer thinks she has a good defense for her client, one of five accused Sept. 11 plotters imprisoned at Guantánamo Bay — if the government ever actually lets the case go to trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/19/magazine/alka-pradhan-v-gitmo.html', 'snippet': 'The human rights lawyer thinks she has a good defense for her client, one of five accused Sept. 11 plotters imprisoned at Guantánamo Bay — if the government ever actually lets the case go to trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Galaxy 19 is a communications satellite that orbits over North America, beaming free-to-air programming to hundreds of thousands of households. It also happens to be the way detainees at Guantánamo Bay get their television. The satellite carries a wealth of religious programming, from “Bible Explorations” to “God’s Learning Channel” to “Global Buddhist Network” — not a lineup well tailored to the particular viewing interests of the Gitmo demographic. What detainees tend to be most interested in is current events, and among the news channels that the satellite carries, RT is one of the most popular. So for lawyers who want their Guantánamo clients to see that their interests are being represented, RT is probably the best option. For that reason, in 2014, a young defense lawyer named Alka Pradhan became a frequent guest on the channel. And because Pradhan is technically an employee of the Department of Defense, her appearances constitute one of countless idiosyncrasies of Gitmo: a contractor for the United States military using a Russian propaganda channel while working for Qaeda terror suspects.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/magazine/24mag-gitmo1/24mag-24gitmo-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/24/magazine/24mag-gitmo1/24mag-24gitmo-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/magazine/24mag-gitmo1/24mag-24gitmo-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/magazine/24mag-gitmo1/24mag-24gitmo-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/magazine/24mag-gitmo1/24mag-24gitmo-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/24/magazine/24mag-gitmo1/24mag-24gitmo-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/magazine/24mag-gitmo1/24mag-24gitmo-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alka Pradhan v. Gitmo', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alka Pradhan v. Gitmo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pradhan, Alka', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extraordinary Rendition', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ali, Ali Abdul Aziz', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-19T10:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey E. Stern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Stern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/118ae6b9-a4f3-54f2-9257-bb825ac4cda7', 'word_count': 7875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/118ae6b9-a4f3-54f2-9257-bb825ac4cda7'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans took aim at graduate students with provisions to tax their benefits. Those were dropped from the tax deal but they could return in a separate bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/19/us/politics/graduate-students-education-tax-bill.html', 'snippet': 'House Republicans took aim at graduate students with provisions to tax their benefits. Those were dropped from the tax deal but they could return in a separate bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samantha Hernandez was finishing up an argument for her dissertation about Latinos and affirmative action on Thursday when the emails started pouring in with the subject line “Congratulations.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/21/us/21dc-grads/19dc-grads-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/21/us/21dc-grads/19dc-grads-articleLarge.j