Taxes (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-19T10:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica L. Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18d02870-3289-5d1a-b467-7964afff681e', 'word_count': 1570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18d02870-3289-5d1a-b467-7964afff681e'}, {'abstract': 'Zingerman’s mail-order Parmigiano-Reggiano club delivers cheese for three months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/19/dining/zingermans-cheese-club.html', 'snippet': 'Zingerman’s mail-order Parmigiano-Reggiano club delivers cheese for three months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Zingerman’s, a delicatessen in Ann Arbor, Mich., they believe that not all Parmigiano-Reggiano cheeses are alike. As proof, they have cheeses imported from some of the more than 300 producers in that Italian region, to show contrasts in taste and texture according to the producer and age. They have started a Parmigiano-Reggiano Club that offers cheeses from different producers in three monthly shipments. The cheeses — Valserena, Roncadella, Borgotaro, La Villa and Cravero — can exhibit typical nuttiness, but some, like the pinkish Roncadella, are sweeter, and others, like La Villa, hint of caramel: Parmigiano-Reggiano Club, $150 for three months, zingermans.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/20/dining/20Burner-Cheese/20Burner-Cheese-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': '