 'Bail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-20T10:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Corbett-Davies, Sharad Goel and Sandra González-Bailón', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corbett-Davies', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sharad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'González-Bailón', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e76650f4-2499-5c99-86a4-9000deb6f016', 'word_count': 1011, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e76650f4-2499-5c99-86a4-9000deb6f016'}, {'abstract': 'Our judges find themselves in the ghastly business of the minute machinery of death — how we prick and poke, slice and cut, and poison the condemned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/20/opinion/executing-terminally-ill-inmates.html', 'snippet': 'Our judges find themselves in the ghastly business of the minute machinery of death — how we prick and poke, slice and cut, and poison the condemned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When judges schedule a lethal injection for a terminally ill prisoner whose struggle against lymphatic cancer and extensive medical history has left him without any easily accessible veins, our law descends into a ghoulish inferno. It is a dreadful place where our most august jurists ruminate over catheter gauges and needle sizes, and ponder whether to slice deep into the groin or puncture internal jugula