etained U.S. citizen suspected of being an Islamic State fighter to Saudi Arabia, where he grew up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/20/us/politics/american-detainee-saudi-arabia.html', 'snippet': 'Security officials are exploring whether to transfer a detained U.S. citizen suspected of being an Islamic State fighter to Saudi Arabia, where he grew up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senior national security officials in the Trump administration are embracing a proposal to transfer to Saudi Arabia an American citizen being held in Iraq as a wartime detainee, according to officials familiar with internal deliberations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials Weigh Sending American Detainee to Saudi Arabia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officials Weigh Sending American Held as ISIS Fighter to Saudi Arabia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Habeas Corpus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-20T23:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage, Eric Schmitt and Adam Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc7b0bd9-3550-55a6-afb6-aab032382b59', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc7b0bd9-3550-55a6-afb6-aab032382b59'}, {'abstract': 'A recent study of hunter-gatherers reminds us that our fictions are more than entertainments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/20/opinion/holiday-stories.html', 'snippet': 'A recent study of hunter-gatherers reminds us that our fictions are more than entertainments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just in time for the holidays, our primary season for collective fictions — Ebenezer Scrooge, the Nutcracker Prince, Santa Claus — a team of researchers has published, in the peer-edited journal Nature Communications, the results of an extensive study of storytelling among the Agta, a contemporary population of hunter-gatherers in the Philippines. The lesson: Stories matter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/21/opinion/21GREENBLATT1/21GREENBLATT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/21/opinion/21GREENBLATT1/21GREENBLATT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/21/opinion/21GREENBLATT1/21GREENBLATT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'su