hat said, story clarity and emotional depth tend to evaporate amid the visual pyrotechnics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22ALONGWITHTHEGODS1/merlin_131286353_8fd0c559-04ce-48ef-8241-07c532e739a7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22ALONGWITHTHEGODS1/merlin_131286353_8fd0c559-04ce-48ef-8241-07c532e739a7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 304}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22ALONGWITHTHEGODS1/merlin_131286353_8fd0c559-04ce-48ef-8241-07c532e739a7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22ALONGWITHTHEGODS1/merlin_131286353_8fd0c559-04ce-48ef-8241-07c532e739a7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1039, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22ALONGWITHTHEGODS1/ALONG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22ALONGWITHTHEGODS1/ALONG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22ALONGWITHTHEGODS1/ALONG1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Along With the Gods’ Is a Fantasy Journey With C.G.I. at Every Turn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Along With the Gods: The Two Worlds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Yong-hwa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Along With the Gods: The Two Worlds (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-21T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/649e221e-d8b5-5601-8352-9ae85a061689', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/649e221e-d8b5-5601-8352-9ae85a061689'}, {'abstract': 'Glenn Close, Julian Sands, Gillian Anderson and Christina Hendricks make up an all-star roster of suspects in this Agatha Christie adaptation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/21/movies/crooked-house-review-glenn-close.html', 'snippet': 'Glenn Close, Julian Sands, Gillian Anderson and Christina Hendricks make up an all-star roster of suspects in this Agatha Christie adaptation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The premise of the murder mystery “Crooked House” is old school: A much-loathed patriarch is sent to his grave, and a houseful of resentful, back-stabbing kinfolk are under suspicion. This intermittently diverting movie is adapted from a 1949 Agatha Christie novel, and it’s several degrees more engaging than another recent Christie-based movie, “Murder on the Orient Express.” But it’s still slight.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/22CROOKED1/merlin_131288639_c6e9f633-3849-4