 to the British Library by Mark Pigott, shed light on Mary’s daily life while imprisoned at Tutbury Castle before her execution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Forty-three letters written by Queen Elizabeth I, her chief minister Lord Burghley and her secretary of state, Sir Francis Walsingham, have been donated to the American Trust for the British Library by Mark Pigott, an American businessman. Mr. Pigott, whose company, Paccar, donated $1.35 million to the British Library in 2008, had previously lent the letters to the library after buying them at an auction in 2010, for around $400,000.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22britishlibrary-item/22britishlibrary-item-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22britishlibrary-item/22britishlibrary-item-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 882}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22britishlibrary-item/22britishlibrary-item-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22britishlibrary-item/22britishlibrary-item-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1393, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22britishlibrary-item/22britishlibrary-item-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22britishlibrary-item/22britishlibrary-item-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22britishlibrary-item/22britishlibrary-item-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Queen Elizabeth Letters Show Her Distrust of Mary Queen of Scots', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Queen Elizabeth I Letters Donated to Trust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Letters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth I, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sadler, Ralph  (1507-87)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mary, Queen of Scots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Library', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tutbury Castle (Staffordshire, England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Trust for the British Library', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-21T18:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e8aa0d-30ff-5b76-82a6-47dde3b20d0d', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e8aa0d-30ff-5b76-82a6-47dde3b20d0d'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Spielberg’s film about the Pentagon Papers is a ticktock thriller that pits freedom of the press — and a tough woman — against the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/21/movies/the-post-review-steven-spielberg-tom-hanks-meryl-streep.html', 'snippet': 'Steven Spielberg’s film about the Pentagon Papers is a ticktock thriller that pits freedom of the press — and a tough woman — against the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Spielberg’s exhilarating drama “The Post” is about a subject that’s dear to the heart of journalists: themselves! Set largely during a few anxious weeks in 1971, it revisits The Washington Post’s decision to publish portions of the Pentagon Papers, an immense classified report that chronicled America’s involvement in Southeast Asia from World War II to 1968. In Mr. Spielberg’s hands, that decision becomes a ticktock thriller about the freedom of the press, the White House’s war on that constitutional right and the middle-aged woman who defended freedom in a fabulous gold caftan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22thepost-2/22thepost-2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22thepost-2/22thepost-2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22thepost-2/22thepost-2-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22thepost-2/22thepost-2-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/arts/22thepost-2/22thepost-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTy