', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/21/nyregion/homeless-program-sharing-stories.html', 'snippet': 'For decades, a group has offered homeless New Yorkers a place to tell the stories of their lives with others who truly understand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Working out her autobiography to deliver in a class, Mona-Lisa Marrero, 48, tried several beginnings, then settled on: “Once upon a time, there was a girl. My name is Mona-Lisa Marrero, and this is my story.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In This Class, Sharing Stories That Once Felt Unspeakable', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Class of Second Chances, Sharing Once-Unspeakable Stories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Charities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-22T00:25:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9490b0d2-e219-553b-8dbf-971944ce64f9', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9490b0d2-e219-553b-8dbf-971944ce64f9'}, {'abstract': 'A proposed Labor Department rule would leave the door open to owners keeping tips for themselves, and could alienate customers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/21/opinion/trump-administration-restaurants-tipping.html', 'snippet': 'A proposed Labor Department rule would leave the door open to owners keeping tips for themselves, and could alienate customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most Americans assume that when they leave a tip for waiters and bartenders, those workers pocket the money. That could become wishful thinking under a Trump administration proposal that would give restaurants and other businesses complete control over the tips earned by their employees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/opinion/22fri2/22fri2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/22/opinion/22fri2/22fri2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/opinion/22fri2/22fri2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/opinion/22fri2/22fri2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1266, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/opinion/22fri2/22fri2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/22/opinion/22fri2/22fri2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/opinion/22fri2/22fri2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trump Administration to Restaurants: Take the Tips!', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content