 and India, they will, they will rock you. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/21/nyregion/the-hindu-bagpipers-of-secaucus.html', 'snippet': 'Like their kilted counterparts in England, Kenya and India, they will, they will rock you. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Secaucus, N.J., if you want to hear Queen’s song “We Will Rock You” performed by three dozen bagpipers and marching drummers in Scottish kilts, the place to go is the Shree Swaminarayan Temple. Ditto for bagpipe renditions of songs from Bollywood soundtracks or traditional Hindu religious music. The Shree Muktajeevan Swamibapa Pipe Band USA, which formed there in 2003, is a younger sibling to pipe bands in England, Kenya and India, where the tradition goes back to the 1950s.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/nyregion/24album41/24album41-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/24/nyregion/24album41/24album41-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/nyregion/24album41/24album41-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/nyregion/24album41/24album41-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/nyregion/24album41/24album41-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/24/nyregion/24a