anted clemency by President Obama, he’s now running his own kitchen in Jersey City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/21/nyregion/a-chef-opens-a-restaurant-his-training-decades-in-a-prison-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'Candido Ortiz served more than 26 years in prison for drug trafficking. Granted clemency by President Obama, he’s now running his own kitchen in Jersey City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERSEY CITY — Candido Ortiz claims he can cook anything: mashed potatoes and gravy, pernil guisado, chicken cacciatore. At his new restaurant here, El Sabor del Cafe, he will honor any request.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chef Opens a Restaurant. His Training? Decades in a Prison Kitchen.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Behind Bars to Behind the Grill, and Savoring the Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGreevey, James E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Sabor Del Cafe (Jersey City, NJ, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ortiz, Candido', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-22T01:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bc909bb-506e-5785-8f19-30ef8433bf01', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bc909bb-506e-5785-8f19-30ef8433bf01'}, {'abstract': 'This film about two brothers searching for their real father can’t decide whether it’s a gross-out comedy or an uplifting tale of brotherly love.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/21/movies/father-figures-review-ed-helms-owen-wilson.html', 'snippet': 'This film about two brothers searching for their real father can’t decide whether it’s a gross-out comedy or an uplifting tale of brotherly love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moviegoers may recall the basic premise of “Father Figures” from “Flirting With Disaster,” a vastly funnier 1996 comedy by David O. Russell. “Father Figures” doesn’t merely flirt. It stars Ed Helms as Peter and Owen Wilson as Kyle, two of the least-related-seeming twins in history. On the day their mother (Glenn Close) marries some cool cat played by Harry Shearer, they learn that their father isn’t dead, as they thought, but just unknown. Mom didn’t practice monogamy in the disco era.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/FATHER1/merlin_131327242_3db35ee8-7d7a-473a-b306-7f25b558df71-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/FATHER1/merlin_131327242_3db35ee8-7d7a-473a-b306-7f25b558df71-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/FATHER1/merlin_131327242_3db35ee8-7d7a-473a-b306-7f25b558df71-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/movies/FATHER1/merlin_13