web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/23/opinion/free-detained-journalists-in-myanmar.html', 'snippet': 'When it comes to press freedom, Myanmar’s new democracy is little different from its old military dictatorship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 13, Myanmar’s Ministry of Information released a photograph of two handcuffed men who had been arrested for simply doing their job. They were Wa Lone and Kyaw Soe Oo, two journalists who work for Reuters and who were arrested on the order of Myanmar’s president, Htin Kyaw, a day earlier on the outskirts of Yangon where they’d gone to meet two policemen from Rakhine State. They haven’t been seen or heard from since.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/opinion/24sun2/merlin_131268606_80ce0167-cc1e-420f-ac39-9ddbf18a3dc2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/24/opinion/24sun2/merlin_131268606_80ce0167-cc1e-420f-ac39-9ddbf18a3dc2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/opinion/24sun2/merlin_131268606_80ce0167-cc1e-420f-ac39-9ddbf18a3dc2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/opinion/24sun2/merlin_131268606_80ce0167-cc1e-420f-ac39-9ddbf18a3dc2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/24/opinion/24sun2/merlin_131268606_80ce0167-cc1e-420f-ac39-9ddbf18a3dc2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wi