ons', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-24T16:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Iuliia Mendel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Iuliia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mendel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ec355dc-5fd1-52e5-8f09-2e75028a5c74', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ec355dc-5fd1-52e5-8f09-2e75028a5c74'}, {'abstract': 'In Aaron Sorkin’s directorial debut, Jessica Chastain plays a gambling entrepreneur running a high-stakes poker game. Much talking, some walking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/24/movies/mollys-game-review-aaron-sorkin-jessica-chastain.html', 'snippet': 'In Aaron Sorkin’s directorial debut, Jessica Chastain plays a gambling entrepreneur running a high-stakes poker game. Much talking, some walking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Words aren’t really exchanged in “Molly’s Game,” Aaron Sorkin’s directorial debut; they’re smashed like racquetballs. Life comes at you fast, and so do the words that rush out of Molly Bloom (Jessica Chastain) as she relays her tale. A poker entrepreneur who ran a high-stakes game before slamming into trouble, Molly is a speed-talker and somewhat of a close one, too. She delivers stretches of her story in a voice-over that suggests that Mr. Sorkin wrote and directed his movie with a stopwatch in one hand and a DVD of Howard Hawks’s motor-mouth comedy “His Girl Friday” in the other.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/arts/25mollysgame1/25mollysgame1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType'