': 'Yale University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cameroon', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-25T00:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tariro Mzezewa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tariro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mzezewa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a697865-cc98-5cd6-a691-c393adc066ac', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a697865-cc98-5cd6-a691-c393adc066ac'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, December 25, 2017.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/24/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-faded-towns-fight-to-rebound-starts-at-the-mall.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, December 25, 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We are not going to sit and wallow. We need to figure out a better future. Don’t tell me it can’t happen.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Faded Town’s Fight to Rebound Starts at the Mall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-12-25T01:12:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd81422e-0f37-5bb9-bc5f-ce3a4c7b96b4', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd81422e-0f37-5bb9-bc5f-ce3a4c7b96b4'}, {'abstract': 'How we should talk about numbers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/24/opinion/2017-wrong-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'How we should talk about numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Israeli intelligence service asked the great psychologist Daniel Kahneman for help in the 1970s, and Kahneman came back with a suggestion: Get rid of the classic intelligence report. It allows leaders to justify any conclusion they want, Kahneman said. In its place, he suggested giving the leaders estimated probabilities of events.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25leonhardtWeb/25leonhardtWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25leonhardtWeb/25leonhardtWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25leonhardtWeb/25leonhardtWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25leonhardtWeb/25leonhardtWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1444, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25leonhardtWeb/25leonhardtWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25leonhardtWeb/25leonhardtWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25leonhardtWeb/25leonhardtWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Was Wrong About This Year', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What I Was  Wrong About  This Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahneman, Daniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Two Thousand Seventeen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-25T01:18:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d3f5e1d-4eb8-5a94-a5dc-01a655785b46', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d3f5e1d-4eb8-5a94-a5dc-01a655785b46'}, {'abstract': '... including the house where Virginia wrote the letter that inspired what is ranked as America’s most “unforgettable” editorial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/24/opinion/santa-manhattan-education.html', 'snippet': '... including the house where Virginia wrote the letter that inspired what is ranked as America’s most “unforgettable” editorial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Santa Claus has a home in New York, in a colonnaded building across from Pennsylvania Station that is the city’s main post office. It must be his home, because that’s where letters addressed to him wind up. The letters come from all over, tens of thousands of them each year, sent by the needy and the hopeful, the luckless and the guileless. Every Christmas season, kindhearted New Yorkers enlist as surrogate Santas. They go to the post office and sift through the mail in search of people to help.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25mon1/25mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25mon1/25mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25mon1/25mon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25mon1/25mon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25mon1/25mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25mon1/25mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/25/opinion/25mon1/25mon1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Santa’s Manhattan Homes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Santa’s Manhattan Homes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':