', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uterine Cancer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-25T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Well', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be228496-5d71-5898-9571-418a8f1291a0', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be228496-5d71-5898-9571-418a8f1291a0'}, {'abstract': 'We followed up with subjects whose stories stuck with us this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/25/us/immigration-opioids.html', 'snippet': 'We followed up with subjects whose stories stuck with us this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a newsy year across the country, filled with hurricanes, shootings, wildfires, marches and more. National correspondents for The New York Times wrote about these events as well as other stories about families and communities grappling with opioid addiction, the federal government’s crackdown on illegal immigration, and on teenagers celebrating prom night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/us/00checkin1/00checkin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/22/us/00checkin1/00checkin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/us/00checkin1/00checkin1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/22/us/