ow the MacLeod family as they enjoy a pleasant holiday in Scotland — in the process somehow awakening a mystical ancient doom. The epidemic that follows, eventually wiping out billions, is described with relentless brutality as governments collapse and things fall apart. In power and poignancy, this segment of “Year One” is a match for end-of-the-world classics like Stephen King’s “The Stand,” Nevil Shute’s “On the Beach” and the better zombie apocalypses.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Otherworldly/31Otherworldly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Otherworldly/31Otherworldly-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 672}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Otherworldly/31Otherworldly-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 915, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Otherworldly/31Otherworldly-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1689, 'width': 1509, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Otherworldly/31Otherworldly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Otherworldly/31Otherworldly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Otherworldly/31Otherworldly-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From ‘Frankenstein’ to Nora Roberts in 200 Years', 'kicker': 'Otherworldly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Year One (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Nora', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Winter of Ice and Iron (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neumeier, Rachel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Heartland (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simo, Ana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Frankenstein: The 1818 Text (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shelley, Mary', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Charlotte', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-26T10:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8e23097-2ee5-59b4-9c20-eaf3d07c8d73', 'word_count': 1325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8e23097-2ee5-59b4-9c20-eaf3d07c8d73'}, {'abstract': 'The Taushiro tribe vanished into the jungles of the Amazon basin in Peru generations ago. Amadeo García García is now the last native speaker of their language.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/26/world/americas/peru-amazon-the-end.html', 'snippet': 'The Taushiro tribe vanished into the jungles of the Amazon basin in Peru generations ago. Amadeo García García is now the last native speaker of their language.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN