m. Bear with him: He wants to learn how to swim so he can learn how to surf so he can improve his core stability and play basketball forever.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/sports/27fabulous1/merlin_131416966_981c6256-925a-4d9b-af53-ffdeaf8e5704-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/27/sports/27fabulous1/merlin_131416966_981c6256-925a-4d9b-af53-ffdeaf8e5704-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/sports/27fabulous1/merlin_131416966_981c6256-925a-4d9b-af53-ffdeaf8e5704-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/sports/27fabulous1/merlin_131416966_981c6256-925a-4d9b-af53-ffdeaf8e5704-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/sports/27fabulous1/27fabulous-web8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/27/sports/27fabulous1/27fabulous-web8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/sports/27fabulous1/27fabulous-web8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fantastical Adventures of Fabulous Flournoy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On a Quest for Eternal Hoops', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flournoy, Fabulous', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Basketball League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newcastle Eagles (Basketball Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-26T19:21:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3635e87c-88e7-508f-897b-40c7fe898c34', 'word_count': 2783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3635e87c-88e7-508f-897b-40c7fe898c34'}, {'abstract': 'In Fatih Akin’s new film, Diane Kruger plays a Hamburg woman who fights for justice and sanity after the murder of her husband and son.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/26/movies/in-the-fade-review-diane-kruger.html', 'snippet': 'In Fatih Akin’s new film, Diane Kruger plays a Hamburg woman who fights for justice and sanity after the murder of her husband and son.', 'lead_paragraph': '“In the Fade,” the new film by Fatih Akin, is divided into three parts. The first two follow a pattern that will be familiar to “Law & Order” fans. A crime is investigated, and then a trial conducted, with a few twists and reversals on the way to the verdict. The emphasis, though, falls less on the procedural aspects of the case than its psychological effects, specifically on Katja Sekerci (Diane Kruger), a German woman whose husband and young son are killed in a bombing in Hamburg.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/arts/27inthefade2/merlin_131495561_e05769ff-ab75-4690-b858-1f559d4cbe3d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/27/arts/27inthefade2/merlin_131495561_e05769ff-ab75-4690-b858-1f559d4cbe3d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/arts/27inthefade2/merlin_131495561_e05769ff-ab75-4690-b858-1f559d4cbe3d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/arts/27inthefade2/merlin_131495561_e05769ff-ab75-4690-b858-1f559d4cbe3d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/arts/27inthefade2/27inthefade2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/27/arts/27inthefade2/27inthefade2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/27/arts/27inthefade2/27inthefade2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘In the Fade’ Is a Tale of Grief and Violence in Modern Germany', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vengeance And Justice Meet Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AKIN, FATIH', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kruger, Diane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'In the Fade (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-26T19:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/50dd150a-1bdd-5480-8710-424bff049bd4', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50dd150a-1bdd-5480-8710-424bff049bd4'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around The Times are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/26/books/review/new-noteworthy-bret-stephens.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around The Times are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE GRAPHIC CANON OF CRIME AND MYSTERY, VOLUME 1 Edited by Russ Kick. (Seven Stories Press, $29.95.) From Poe to Kafka to Dostoyevsky, all the masters are here, in these short, graphic renderings of the darkest, most foreboding writing of all time. With different artists and illustrators taking on each tale, there are many revelations. TIME OF GRATITUDE By Gennady Aygi. (New Directions, $16.95.) This collection of poetry and verse-infused prose from the celebrated Russian and Chuvash poet bows to the writers and artists who kept him creatively inspired during the Soviet era. YOU & ME & WHY WE ARE IN LOVE By Aurelia Alcaïs. (Penguin, $15.) Love comes in many flavors and Alcaïs, a French actress and illustrator, tries to capture many of them in her basic but sweet portraits of variations like “inquiring love,” “qualified love” and “modern love.” THE THREE MUSKETEERS By Alexandre Dumas. (Pegasus Books, $26.95.) The classic French epic in a new translation by Lawrence Ellsworth brings freshness to the story of d’Artagnan and his pals. THE RUIN OF KASCH By Roberto Calasso. (Farrar, Straus & Giroux, $17.) Calasso’s nearly four-decade project, eclectic and erudite, to tell the intellectual history of the modern world began with this first book in the series, about the French Revolution and so much more, translated anew into English.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31NewNoteworthy1/31NewNoteworthy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31NewNoteworthy1/31NewNoteworthy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31NewNoteworthy1/31NewNoteworthy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31NewNoteworthy1/31NewNoteworthy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1364, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31NewNoteworthy1/31NewNoteworthy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31NewNoteworthy1/31NewNoteworthy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20