 proposition. But nowadays it is more essential than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/29/books/review/technology-politics-fiction.html', 'snippet': 'For fiction writers, keeping up with technological and political change in their work is a risky proposition. But nowadays it is more essential than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every novel is a letter written to the future. The words we write often don’t appear in print for a year, two years, even more — and by the time they appear, the world (which we are supposed to be reflecting) has changed. Increasingly, as history seems to speed up, novelists have to ask themselves hard questions about how they’ll possibly keep pace.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Anderson-SUB01/31Anderson-SUB01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Anderson-SUB01/31Anderson-SUB01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Anderson-SUB01/31Anderson-SUB01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Anderson-SUB01/31Anderson-SUB01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1044, 'width': 1469, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/31/books/review/31Anderson-SUB01/31Anderson-SUB01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnai