es)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mazda Motor Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Cars (Compact, Subcompact and Microcars)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-29T23:32:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9a8c809-29fb-574f-be57-13c9256c84a8', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9a8c809-29fb-574f-be57-13c9256c84a8'}, {'abstract': 'At the site of a deadly fire from a decade ago, a rebuilt home disguises the terrible loss of 10 people, nine of them children, but a mother remembers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/29/nyregion/2007-bronx-fire-magassa-repeats-itself-with-deadly-force.html', 'snippet': 'At the site of a deadly fire from a decade ago, a rebuilt home disguises the terrible loss of 10 people, nine of them children, but a mother remembers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To a stranger’s knock, a boy of about 9 opens the door of 1022 Woodycrest Avenue, the Bronx. He listens for a moment, then circles back to summon his mother, Manthia Magassa. The warming fragrance of a stew has drifted from the kitchen, then streams in to the cold doorway. An electronic chirp sounds from the wooden stairwell. The boy watches television.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/30/nyregion/30ABOUT/30ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': '