 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/30/us/politics/30dc-factcheck/merlin_131701871_655f3749-9330-4e3c-aff7-696e82f34fb5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/30/us/politics/30dc-factcheck/merlin_131701871_655f3749-9330-4e3c-aff7-696e82f34fb5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/30/us/politics/30dc-factcheck/merlin_131701871_655f3749-9330-4e3c-aff7-696e82f34fb5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/30/us/politics/30dc-factcheck/merlin_131701871_655f3749-9330-4e3c-aff7-696e82f34fb5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/30/us/politics/30dc-factcheck/30dc-factcheck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/30/us/politics/30dc-factcheck/30dc-factcheck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/30/us/politics/30dc-factcheck/30dc-factcheck-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '10 Falsehoods From Trump’s Interview With The Times', 'kicker': 'Fact Check', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Much That Wasn’t True in a 30-Minute Interview', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-30T00:09:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Qiu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qiu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0322caad-6e4e-5bc0-a8d4-c75862b717c5', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0322caad-6e4e-5bc0-a8d4-c75862b717c5'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Eric Ripert adds an eight-course meat-free option to the tasting menu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/29/dining/le-bernardin-adds-a-vegetarian-tasting-menu.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Eric Ripert adds an eight-course meat-free option to the tasting menu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has always been an occasional vegetable or meat dish served at Le Bernardin, which has featured mostly seafood from the day Maguy and Gilbert Le Coze opened it in Paris in 1972. Now Eric Ripert, the restaurant’s executive chef since 1994 and then partner, is introducing the restaurant’s first vegetarian tasting menu. “I often get a dozen inquiries a week for a vegetable tasting,” he said. “I like the idea of a menu that pays homage to the vegetable, though it’s a creative challenge.” The menu has six savory courses and two desserts. Standouts include celeriac soup served in a whole celeriac, a twist of pasta thatched with black truffles, a roulade of zucchini and caponata, and roasted porcini alongside eggplant that is both silky and crisp: Vegetarian tasting menu, $185 a person, Le Bernardin, 155 West 51st Street (Seventh Avenue), 212-554-1515, le-bernardin.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/dining/03burnerbernardin/03burnerbernardin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/03/dining/03burnerbernardin/03burnerbernardin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/dining/03burnerbernardin/03burnerbernardin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/dining/03burnerbernardin/03burnerbernardin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/dining/03burnerbernardin/03burnerbernardin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/03/dining/03burnerbernardin/03burnerbernardin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/dining/03burnerbernardin/03burnerbernardin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Le Bernardin Adds a Vegetarian Tasting Menu', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: A Vegetarian Tasting Menu Is Added at Le Bernardin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetarianism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Bernardin (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ripert, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-12-30T00:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44be51cd-75c1-509c-a49a-81efa5bc056b', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44be51cd-75c1-509c-a49a-81efa5bc056b'}, {'abstract': 'Constance Kirker, a culinary historian, will give a talk on sweets role in Christianity, Hinduism, Buddhism and Islam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/12/29/dining/religious-symbolism-candy-culinary-historian.html', 'snippet': 'Constance Kirker, a culinary historian, will give a talk on sweets role in Christianity, Hinduism, Buddhism and Islam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the religious side of the holiday season, and indeed across the calendar, there are any number of traditional sweets with sacred meanings. Constance Kirker, a culinary historian and retired professor of art history at Penn State who now teaches at the Culinary Institute of America in Singapore, will address the topic “Sacred Sweet Tooth: The Symbolism and Function of Candy and Sweets in Religious Traditions” as it pertains to Christianity, Hinduism, Buddhism and Islam. The talk is sponsored by the Culinary Historians of New York. Sweets will be served: “Sacred Sweet Tooth,” Jan. 15 at 6:30 p.m., $25 for members, $40 for nonmembers, $10 for students, eventbrite.com; Culinary Historians of New York, Anthroposophic